Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(update-pause): one pause-note prefix; a
 transient owner-forward failure keeps the backoff

Follow-up to PR #2167 review 5890829579 (t_01a1d4d34f148c5a), card t_01a1d4d9966a5a40.

1. One prefix. tui_gateway.session_history now imports update_pause.PAUSE_REPLAY_NOTE_PREFIX
   (update_pause loads only the stdlib) instead of keeping its own copy. The gateway's auto-continue
   note recognition moves to gateway/run_auto_continue_noise.py (re-exported from gateway.run; keeps
   run.py under its FILE_LINES cap) with a named _PAUSE_REPLAY_NOTE_PREFIX instead of an inline
   literal. It stays literal so the gateway never imports tui_gateway at load;
   tests/gateway/test_auto_continue_note_prefixes.py pins the gateway prefixes to the tui ones and runs
   _strip_auto_continue_noise on real pause_note(...) output: plain, later-turns, queued, chain
   (pauses >= 2), unknown-old, and with a job report + carried note trailing the request.
2. _paused_turn_to_ledger_owner: a forward the owner turned away before queuing anything for a
   passing reason (OwnerUnavailable such as "did not admit it", runtime_draining / stale_epoch /
   admission_conflict / queue_full refusals, an OSError dial failure) no longer retires the pause:
   it returns False, so the caller's 30 s backoff retries the forward, up to OWNER_FORWARD_TRIES (3)
   per pause; then it is retired with the attempt count logged. OwnerNotRunning, definitive refusals
   (permission_denied, profile_mismatch, not_found, runtime_retired, invalid_params) and unexpected
   errors still retire at once; OwnerUnconfirmed is never retried (it may already be queued).
3. pause_note: drop the redundant `paused_at is not None` (stale implies it).

Tests: RED on the PR #2167 head (new tests: 6 failed + 1 import error), GREEN here; 32 related files
(update_pause*, auto_continue, turn_marker, owner_forward, session_history, gateway stripper users):
416 passed.
